We need to find the GCD of all n numbers, then count how many numbers are not multiples of that GCD. If all numbers are multiples of the GCD, then removing any one number will increase the GCD, so the answer is 1. Otherwise, we need to remove all numbers that are not multiples of the GCD, so the answer is the count of those numbers.

